  "id": "collinearity",
  "term": "collinearity",
  "definition": "Collinearity is a situation in which measured variables are so strongly related that their unique associations become hard to separate in a statistical model. In this study context, high collinearity was taken as a sign of possible construct overlap and a reason to interpret unexpected coefficients cautiously.",
